WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/BatteryComparison.tsx — the fleet "Battery Status" panel:
    Props : { vehicles: Vehicle[] } (useVehicles upstream).
    Data  : useQuery(['fleet-battery-states', ids]) fans out one fetchVehicleState(id) per vehicle
            (battery_level + rated_range, both SI), refetchInterval 30_000; a per-vehicle try/catch maps a
            failure to `state: null`. useTranslation('vehicles'), useUnits (formatDistance).
    Body  : bars = allStates.filter(q => q.state !== null)
            if (bars.length === 0) return null                                   // → P4 `.empty`
            <GlassPanel> <h3><Activity/> t('fleet.batteryStatus','Fleet Battery Status') </h3>
              bars.map(({vehicle, state}) =>
                 level = state.battery_level ?? 0;  color = batteryColor(level);  width = `${level}%`;
                 name  = vehicle.display_name || vehicle.vin;  range = formatDistance(state.rated_range ?? 0))
    Helpers (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
            batteryColor(level)      = level > 60 ? #10b981 : level > 25 ? #f59e0b : #ef4444   (lib/colors.ts);
            formatDistance(m, pref)  = !finite ? (pref.emptyDisplay ?? '—')
                                       : `${Intl.NumberFormat(pref.locale,{min=max=digits}).format(
                                            convertDistanceFromSI(m, pref.distance))} ${pref.distance}`,
                                       digits = resolvePrecision(pref.precision, 1)  (lib/unitConversion.ts);
            convertDistanceFromSI    = km: m/1000 · mi: m/1609.344 · ft: m/0.3048.
    i18n  : the source makes ONE t() call — t('fleet.batteryStatus','Fleet Battery Status') (ns "vehicles").
            Per the native no-English-literals rule the key is preserved verbatim and every remaining literal
            (the `${level}%` template + the P4 leaf chrome) is promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "BatteryComparison").

